{
  "statement": {
    "index": 1,
    "modal": "Must",
    "text": "judge-jev MUST support the target mode `prompt`."
  },
  "record": {
    "id": "REQ-JEV-0203",
    "title": "Target modes",
    "status": "Draft",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "created": "2026-11-07",
    "last_updated": "2026-11-08",
    "owner": "Rand Lee",
    "supersedes": null,
    "superseded_by": null,
    "requirement_statement": {
      "text": "Definitions: A mode (target mode) names what a location holds: `prompt`\n(prompt text), `skill` (a skill file), `task` (a task template) or `code`\n(source code). A location is the text judged against a record: a whole file\n(`path`), a Markdown section (`path#Heading`) or a code symbol\n(`path::Symbol`) (REQ-JEV-0207). sc-compose is the template renderer; in\nstrict mode it fails on any template variable the vars file does not set. A\nvars file holds the values of a template's variables. An assignment is the\ntext a task template renders to. sc-agent is the agent tool whose Rust Jev\ntool will replace judge-jev's Python Jev core (ADR-JEV-0007). Tree-sitter\ngrammars are the parsers that find a named symbol in source code.",
      "statements": [
        {
          "modal": "Must",
          "text": "judge-jev MUST support the target mode `prompt`."
        },
