    "supersedes": null,
    "superseded_by": null,
    "requirement_statement": {
      "text": "Definitions: A question IRI (Internationalized Resource Identifier) is the\nURN that names a question, such as `urn:judge-jev:question:req.term`. A tree\nfile is a Turtle file of quality decision trees. A consumer extension is a\ntree file that a repository using judge-jev adds. `jj:id` is a question's\nshort id within its tree.",
      "statements": [
        {
          "modal": "Must",
          "text": "Every question IRI in one scope (by default the repository) MUST be\ndeclared in one tree file only, across judge-jev's trees and every\nconsumer extension's."
        },
        {
          "modal": "Must",
          "text": "Every `jj:id` in judge-jev's trees and in every consumer extension's\nMUST be unique within its tree."
        }
      ]
    },
    "rationale": "A question's identity is its IRI.\n\nRand Lee, 2026-11-08: \"We would need to make sure all questions in\njudge-jev AND in consumer extensions follow a naming policy for uniqueness\nw/in that scope (repo is typical scope).\"",
